Subject: px5g-mbedtls: fixes for the certificates it writes

The tool that makes the router's own HTTPS certificate:

- an IPv4 address in subjectAltName was written as a zero padded IPv6
  address, so clients refused the certificate for that address; several
  addresses all carried the last one;
- with no subjectAltName at all the extension was written empty, which
  Chrome refuses outright;
- an -addext value it does not support stopped the option parser, so the
  options after it were ignored without an error;
- the default RSA key is 2048 bit; with the old default of 512 mbedtls
  refused to make a key at all.

OpenWrt commits 54d2eb96a1, 9cad8741a7 and a31b1b75cb, taken as they
are.

